ed y Parc Cwm at Parc le Breos, it represents an important example of Neolithic burial architecture in South Wales.[1]'' -> ''Parc Cwm long cairn, also known as Parc le Breos burial chamber, is a partly restored Neolithic chambered tomb on the Gower Peninsula, Wales [1]. Identified in 1937 as a Severn-Cotswold type of chambered long barrow, it was built around 5,850 years before present during the early Neolithic [1]. The monument features a trapezoidal cairn of rubble with a cromlech (megalithic burial chamber) [1]. Located approximately 12 km west-south-west of Swansea in Coed y Parc Cwm at Parc le Breos, it represents an important example of Neolithic burial architecture in South Wales [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304714", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc le Breos, Gwyr o''r de.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc_le_Breos,_Gwyr_y_cwrt.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc_le_Breos,_Gwyr_y_cwrt.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc le Breos, Gwyr o''r de.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306800", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc le Breos, Gwyr o''r de.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/06b8aeb4/Parc_le_Breos,_Gwyr_y_cwrt.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
