ounced the claims.'' -> ''Named by Semir Osmanagic in 2005 as part of his pseudoarchaeological pyramid claims, the hill is composed of layers of sandstone, clay, mudstone, and siltstone deposited in an ancient lake system during the Miocene (5-23 million years ago) [1] [2] [3]. Scientists have identified the formation as a flatiron, and the European Association of Archaeologists has denounced the claims [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
