lay metopes with yellow veneer, spearheads, and part of the arm of a marble statue [1]. One important artifact is a bronze phiale in excellent condition with the inscription \"Tilephilos dedicated me to Herakles\" in the archaic Greek alphabet [1]. This indicates the presence of a Herakles cult, which is linked to Pherae and is documented in the region through Hellenistic-era inscriptions [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116195", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116196", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247438", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348084", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348085", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
