    ('49d6b7c5-e692-4e51-845f-304cad53f3af'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:49d6b7c5-e692-4e51-845f-304cad53f3af:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: antiquity ''5'' restored on Alabanda', '72383c565975747af82f5458795d0dfd', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -500"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83538", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2083:chunk-0001: description ''Alabanda (or Antiochia of the Chrysaorians) was an ancient Carian city in Anatolia, located near modern Doğanyurt, Çine, in Aydın Province, Turkey [1]. The site features notable remains including a theatre with massive carved pillars from the Hellenistic period [2]. While excavations have uncovered architectural fragments, very few inscriptions have been found at the site [3]. The city was situated in the historical region of Caria, which lay between ancient Lycia and Ionia, reflecting the cultural blending typical of southwestern Anatolia.'' -> ''Alabanda or Antiochia of the Chrysaorians was a city of ancient Caria, Anatolia, the site of which is near Doğanyurt, Çine, Aydın Province [1]. The name reverted to Alabanda after the Seleucid defeat at the Battle of Magnesia in 190 BC [1]. The ruins of Alabanda are 8 km west of Çine and consist of the remains of a theatre and several other buildings, but excavations have yielded very few inscriptions [1]. The names of some bishops of Alabanda are known because they participated in church councils [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98123", "url"