ial chamber, Kilmartin, Aug 1974 (51700821612).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:336997", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4306:chunk-0001: description ''Nether Largie South is a Neolithic chambered cairn in Kilmartin Glen, part of a linear cemetery of five burial cairns[1]. Probably dating from the fourth millennium BC, it was originally around 40 metres in diameter and 4 metres high, though stone robbing has reduced its size. The internal chamber, subdivided into four compartments by floor slabs, is over 6 metres long. Some stones bear cup and ring marks, a characteristic of prehistoric carved stone in the glen[2].'' -> ''Nether Largie South is a Neolithic chambered cairn in Kilmartin Glen, part of a linear cemetery of five burial cairns [1] [2]. The internal chamber, subdivided into four compartments by floor slabs, is over 6 metres long [1] [3].''"}]'::jsonb),
