59", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4307:chunk-0001: description \"The Tsagaan Salaa rock paintings comprise one of the largest rock art complexes in North and Central Asia, located in western Mongolia''s Altai Tavan Bogd National Park. Spanning roughly 15 square kilometres along the White River Valley, the site contains over 10,000 figures dating from the Neolithic (c. 11,000 BC) through the Bronze Age to the Turkic period. Imagery documents the transition from big-game hunting to pastoral herding and horse-dependent nomadism. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the Petroglyphic Complexes of the Mongolian Altai.\" -> ''The Tsagaan Salaa rock paintings comprise one of the largest rock art complexes in North and Central Asia [1]. Spanning roughly 15 square kilometres along the White River Valley, the site contains over 10,000 figures [2] [3] [4]. Imagery documents the transition from big-game hunting to pastoral herding and horse-dependent nomadism [3] [5]. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the Petroglyphic Complexes of the Mongolian Altai [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385745", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385746", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4df3dcbd-62d3-4e37-92fe-e79989233f1f'::uuid, 'antiquity', '2', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:4df3dcbd-62d3-4e37-92fe-e79989233f1f:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: antiquity ''5'' restored on La Pintada', '8a5bbfc5d8f84af633362160f50e613d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 2 from period_start 500"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83800", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2086:chunk-0001: description ''La Pintada is an archaeological site in the Sierra Libre, about 60 km south of Hermosillo, Sonora, Mexico, considered one of the most important cave painting areas in northwestern Mexico. The canyon contains over 2,500 catalogued rock art images including cave paintings and engravings depicting animals such as birds, deer, and reptiles, believed to be cosmo-vision representations created about 1,200 years ago. The site served diverse groups including hunter-gatherers during the 12th-13th centuries and later Seri, Yaqui, and Pima peoples who used it as a ritual center between the 17th-18th centuries. Outside the canyon, seasonal camping grounds attest to prolonged occupation.'' -> ''La Pintada is an archaeological site located some 60 kilometers south of the city of Hermosillo, Sonora, Mexico, within the \"La Pintada\" canyon, part of the \"Sierra Libre\" [1]. La Pintada comprises two different archaeological components; within the Canyon are cave paintings and rock engravings, while outside, on the alluvial plain of the Canyon are vestiges of various seasonal camping grounds in an extensive area, characterized by a concentration of archaeological material: ceramic, stone tools [1]. Most of the archaeological materials found in these grounds, are within the archaeological tradition known as Central Coast, and are particularly similar to those found by Edward Mosler and Thomas Bowen at sites in the region of Tastiota and Punta San Antonio in the southern part of the Central Coast area [1]. So far, La Pintada is the site associated with that archaeological tradition farther away from the coastline [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98173", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98174", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149419", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4df3dcbd/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248282", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348217", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348218", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:413999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07d_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:414000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07d_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''500''"}]'::jsonb),
