pproximately 1st century AD), it features a unique spiral staircase cut into the interior walls for descending to the water level. Underground tunnels and rock-carved channels once supplied surrounding farmland, demonstrating sophisticated Nabataean water engineering. The well''s name derives from the Canaanite military commander Sisera mentioned in the Hebrew Bible.\" -> \"The Sisira Well is an ancient well carved out of sandstone, located north of Sakaka near Zabal Castle in the Al-Jawf region of Saudi Arabia [1]. Underground tunnels and rock-carved channels once supplied surrounding farmland [1]. The well''s name derives from the Canaanite military commander Sisera mentioned in the Hebrew Bible [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348227", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348228", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('50debb04-ae49-4d55-9756-bdfb8fbacf9c'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:50debb04-ae49-4d55-9756-bdfb8fbacf9c:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: antiquity ''5'' restored on Siscia', '506112b694d2dacea69e7b99fcef7d9f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -500"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80844", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2010:chunk-0001: description \"Siscia, modern-day Sisak in Croatia, was a major Roman city at the confluence of the Kupa, Sava, and Odra rivers. Captured by Octavian in 35 BC after a thirty-day siege, it was elevated to colonia status by Vespasian as Colonia Flavia Siscia. The city housed the state mint and treasury in the 3rd-4th centuries and served as capital of Pannonia Savia. Excavations have revealed bath buildings, walls, inscriptions, and stamped tiles reading ''SISC(ia)'', though much of ancient Siscia lies beneath the modern town.\" -> ''Siscia is described by Roman writers as a great town in the south of Upper Pannonia, on the southern bank of the Savus, on an island formed by that river and two others, the Colapis and Odra, a canal dug by Tiberius completing the island [1]. It was on the great road from Aemona to Sirmium [1]. Siscia was from the first a strongly fortified town; and after its capture by Tiberius, in the reign of Augustus, it became one of the most important places of Pannonia; for being on two navigable rivers, it not only carried on considerable commerce, but became the central point from which Augustus and Tiberius carried on their undertakings against the Pannonians and Illyrians [1]. Tiberius did much to enlarge and embellish the town, which as early as that time seems to have been made a colonia, for Pliny mentions it as such: in the time of Septimius Severus it received fresh colonists [1]. The town contained an imperial mint, which produced coins under a series of emperors between 262 and 383 AD [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98855", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Sisak_Fortress.jpg/400px-Sisak_Fortress.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/50debb04/Roman_ruins_in_Sisak.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248301", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248302", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348237", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:414001", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07d_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:414002", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07d_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''-500''"}]'::jsonb),
