_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4310:chunk-0001: description \"Kinal is a major pre-Columbian Maya archaeological site in the Petén Department of northern Guatemala. The site''s major occupational phase dates to the Late Classic period (600-900 AD), with evidence of a substantial expansionary building program during the first half of the 8th century AD[1][2]. The architectural style corresponds to the Late Classic period. Kinal was discovered in the 1960s by archaeologist Ian Graham during a regional survey, though no excavations were conducted at that time[1][2].\" -> \"Kinal is a major pre-Columbian Maya archaeological site in the Petén Department of northern Guatemala [1]. The site''s major occupational phase dates to the Late Classic period (600-900 AD), with evidence of a substantial expansionary building program during the first half of the 8th century AD [1]. The architectural style corresponds to the Late Classic period [1]. Kinal was discovered in the 1960s by archaeologist Ian Graham during a regional survey, though no excavations were conducted at that time [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349018", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349019", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384249", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4401:chunk-0001: description \"Kinal is a major pre-Columbian Maya archaeological site in the Petén Department of northern Guatemala [1]. The site''s major occupational phase dates to the Late Classic period (600-900 AD), with evidence of a substantial expansionary building program during the first half of 