nes have been found, from at least 324 individuals, but no intact skeletons [1]. Mixed with the human bones were talons and bones from eight to 20 birds [1]. Some believed that the eagle was a totem animal for the individuals entombed here, but subsequent research indicated that the bird artifacts were added at a later time [1]. These were identified as predominantly belonging to the white-tailed sea eagle (Haliaeetus albicilla) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150341", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Isbister_Cairn_Tomb_of_the_Eagles_04.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5aaf8925/Isbister Chambered Cairn 20110524.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5aaf8925/Isbister Chambered Cairn 20110524.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5aaf8925/Isbister_Cairn_Tomb_of_the_Eagles_04.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
