ne circles and cairns around the Long Meg site that includes the circle at Glassonby, Old Parks, and other sites since lost [1]. Two of the stones (only one remaining) were decorated in antiquity with a series of concentric circles and a spiral [1]. When first discovered in the middle of the nineteenth century, there was a c.1.3m mound covering the stones [1]. Bones, charcoal and a ''coarse pot'' were found buried in a cist at the centre of the circle [1]. Two stones found in the cist (now in Penrith Museum), have cup and ring markings [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118955", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118956", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118957", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Stone circle'' -> ''Cairn''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249703", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249704", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349925", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349926", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385860", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
