rded natural protection from mass incursions into imperial territory, with the exception of a gap stretching roughly from Mogontiacum (now Mainz) on the Rhine to Castra Regina [1]. The limes itself is a relatively simple construction [1]. The limes had a deeper ditch and a higher mound than a camp fortification [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120250", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154635", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/86066b6b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/86066b6b/Hansselmann Fortsetzung Beweiss.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313815", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/86066b6b/Hansselmann Fortsetzung Beweiss.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/86066b6b/Rätische_Mauer,_WP_12-77.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
