    ('9755c087-8b24-46e2-9785-b5ac6c91f3ea'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:9755c087-8b24-46e2-9785-b5ac6c91f3ea:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: mystery ''5'' restored on Moray', 'd9ab50f617ee3dd3df3c26912f9cfe9f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Archaeological site'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0319:chunk-0001: site_type ''Geological interest'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0100:chunk-0001: description ''Moray is an Inca archaeological site on a high plateau at 3,500 m elevation, northwest of Cusco, Peru, featuring concentric circular terraces descending up to 150 m deep. Believed to have functioned as an agricultural research laboratory, each terrace created its own microclimate with temperature differences of up to 15 degrees C between top and bottom. The Inca imported soils from diverse regions and tested over 250 plant species including potatoes, quinoa, and maize. Discovered from the air in 1932, the site may date in part to the earlier Wari culture (6th-10th c.).'' -> ''Moray (Quechua: Muray) is an archaeological site in Peru approximately 50 kilometres northwest of Cuzco on a high plateau at about 3,500 metres and just west of the village of Maras [1]. The site contains Inca ruins, mostly consisting of several terraced circular depressions, the largest of which is approximately 30 m deep [1]. As with many other Inca sites, it also has an irrigation system [1]. The purpose of these depressions is uncertain, but their depth, design, and orientation with respect to wind and sun creates a temperature difference of as much as 15 °C between the top and the bottom [1]. The wide temperature differences in the terraces have created microclimates, similar to what is achieved in greenhouses in modern times [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Moray_-_Qechuyoq.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9755c087/Moray, 2023 (13).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:332705", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9755c087/Moray, 2023 (13).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9755c087/Moray - Qechuyoq.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
