ivilian settlement, or canaba, grew around the fortress [1]. Chester''s Roman Amphitheatre, south-east of the fortress, is the largest-known military amphitheatre in Britain [1]. The civilian settlement remained after the Romans departed, eventually becoming the present-day city of Chester [1]. The fortress contained barracks, granaries, headquarters, military baths, and an unusual elliptical building which had it been finished may have been intended to act as the governor of Britain''s headquarters [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156716", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/Camp de légion de Deva Victrix.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/Camp de légion de Deva Victrix.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/ChesterCan4.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9c1414b7-dda6-4bbc-ad6f-541dd811763d'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:9c1414b7-dda6-4bbc-ad6f-541dd811763d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: mystery ''5'' restored on Qollmay', '1abbaa0e2f3570e341f6904c00517445', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Archaeological site'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2139:chunk-0001: description \"Qollmay (also Qullmay) is an Inca Empire archaeological site in Peru''s Cusco Region, featuring multiple buildings constructed along a granite cliff at 3,436 m elevation. Located 4 km northwest of Chinchaypujio on the road to Sumaru, the structures are believed to have served both administrative and religious functions.\" -> ''Qollmay is 4 km North-West (about a 25-minute drive on dirt road) of Chinchaypujio [1]. First excavated by Max Uhle in 1905 and registered by Ken Heffernan in 1986, it has been classified in 6 sectors and has about a dozen foundations, half a dozen well preserved walls and one well preserved walled-off natural cavern with Inca-style stonework inside, located within sector 1 [1]. This cavernous building is thought to be the most important one in the whole site [1]. Adjacent to it is a rock formation reminiscent of a birth canal, speculated to be the site of fertility rituals [1]. The site is embedded within Inca-made, rectangular terraces, now overgrown with grass [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104349", "url": "r