capstone, 4 metres by 2.5 metres, and 0.5 metres thick, is supported partly by the rising ground, partly by two upright stones; another upright to the east has fallen away [1]. The chamber is partly below ground [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107912", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107913", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160845", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c17fcb7a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c17fcb7a/King’s Quoit (DSC07903).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252844", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387345", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
