ooktown [1]. The paintings are generally large and well preserved, and engravings of great antiquity occur [1]. Engravings of both figurative and abstract styles are found throughout Quinkan country [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108731", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-25000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162111", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/Quinkan5.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253233", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253234", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/Quinkan5.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('cac95409-52f9-4a26-bf59-fd7af98d054e'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-07d-rollback:cac95409-52f9-4a26-bf59-fd7af98d054e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07d: mystery ''9'' restored on Anim Synagogue', 'd82ce6298f14193a37519f9734b0cd7c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Religious'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 3 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export ddb8b67997033964 (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 118 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07c''s own export (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87464", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2172:chunk-0001: description ''A 4th-7th century CE basilical synagogue at Horvat Anim (Khirbet Ghuwein al-Tahta) in the southern Hebron Hills, Israel. The rectangular hall measures approximately 14.5 by 8.5 metres, oriented toward Jerusalem, with hewn stone walls surviving to 3.5 metres. Excavated by Z. Ilan and Dan Urman in 1988-89, revealing preserved eastern lintels, mosaic pavement traces beneath a later stone floor, and inscription fragments. Later converted to a mosque in the early Islamic period. The site reflects the large Jewish village of Anaya during the Roman-Byzantine era.'' -> ''The site is identified with the lower of the two historical settlements known as Anim/Anaia from Biblical times and Late Antiquity and preserves the remains of the Anim Synagogue [1]. Archaeological remains of a rectangular, basilical synagogue date its main phase to the 4th–7th centuries CE, with later conversion to a mosque in the early Islamic period [1]. Excavations by Z. Ilan and Dan Urman (1988–89) reported standing hewn-stone walls to c. 3.5 m, an eastern entrance with preserved lintels, traces of a mosaic pavement beneath a later stone floor, and inscription fragments [1]. The synagogue at Lower ʽAnim is paired historically with a Byzantine-era church on the hill east of Upper ʽAnim, reflecting the Christianisation patterns of the South Hebron Hills in late antiquity [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Religious''"}]'::jsonb),
