 a mosaic pavement beneath a later stone floor, and inscription fragments [1]. The synagogue at Lower ʽAnim is paired historically with a Byzantine-era church on the hill east of Upper ʽAnim, reflecting the Christianisation patterns of the South Hebron Hills in late antiquity [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Religious''"}]'::jsonb),
