 Age settlements in Britain, in extent if not necessarily in population [1]. Stanwick was the site of Sir Mortimer Wheeler''s last major archaeological excavation in Britain, which he carried out over the summers of 1951 and 1952 [1]. Amongst Wheeler''s most famous finds at Stanwick were an Iron Age sword, unusually still in its well-preserved ash wood scabbard, and the nearby skull of a severed head [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163051", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-029: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/Wheeler%27s_Wall.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d34a4c75/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
