cle is situated on the summit of Tops Hill [1]. Several stones are cupmarked [1]. A single ‘outlier’ stone about 2 metres high stands to the southeast of the circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109735", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109736", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163811", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/da99f5e5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/da99f5e5/01. Beltany Stone Circle, Co. Donegal.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/da99f5e5/01. Beltany Stone Circle, Co. Donegal.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/da99f5e5/Beltany_Stone_Circle_P1180130.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
